                            "Having an affinity or fondness for flesh."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2bf591ea-427f-43a7-8076-2a0dba9f6a87",
                                "sense_id": "68f92215-218a-3423-a9d5-f47499bcf382",
                                "text": "Mr. A. E. Ellis is of the opinion that it is sarcophilous, being so abundant amongst bones in old graves; Gray (1840, 192) refers to its presence in Saxon coffins."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3a3f54ae-8d43-40f7-9b9f-0c5b5a8e0cc2",
                                "sense_id": "68f92215-218a-3423-a9d5-f47499bcf382",
                                "text": "Indian Romeos […] have yielded to the temptation to pat, feel, pinch and brush against the more irresistible and accessible portions of women who come within discreet cop-a-feel distance.\nHowever sarcophilous the Indian gentlemen are, the ladies are taking umbrage to such familiarity and have accomplished two things. One is a well-motivated desire to study self-defense and various forms of martial arts."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
